CM_ SG_ 1029 Vq "Imaginary component of the applied non-rotating voltage vector to the motor.";
CM_ SG_ 1030 Id "Real component of the applied non-rotating current vector to the motor. This vector represents the field current of the motor.";
CM_ SG_ 1030 Iq "Imaginary component of the applied non-rotating current vector to the motor. This current produces torque in the motor and should be in phase with the back-EMF of the motor";
CM_ SG_ 1031 BEMFd "By definition this value is always 0V.";
CM_ SG_ 1031 BEMFq "The peak of the phase to neutral motor voltage.";
CM_ SG_ 1032 Supply15V "Actual voltage level of the 15V power rail.";
CM_ SG_ 1033 Supply3V3 "Actual voltage level of the 3.3V power rail.";
CM_ SG_ 1033 Supply1V9 "Actual voltage level of the 1.9V DSP power rail.";
CM_ SG_ 1036 DspBoardTemp "Temperature of the DSP board.";
CM_ SG_ 1038 DCBusAh "Charge flow into the controller DC bus from the time of reset.";
CM_ SG_ 1038 Odometer "Distance the vehicle has travelled since reset.";
CM_ SG_ 1047 SlipSpeed "Slip speed when driving an induction motor.";
CM_ BO_ 1039 "Mode command, base+0x0F, PC to controller. Four u16 LE words [0, 0, mode, start]. Select a mode with start 0, then send [0,0,0,1] to start the acquisition. All zero = back to normal mode. PhasorSense and the extraction modes ENERGISE THE MOTOR PHASES. No handshake or unlock. Replies on 0x410/0x411. Not part of the config transfer.";
CM_ SG_ 1039 Start "1 starts the acquisition for the mode selected by the previous frame.";
CM_ SG_ 1039 Mode "0 normal, 1 PhasorSense, 2 parameter extraction, 3 induction motor extraction.";
CM_ BO_ 1040 "Acquisition status, base+0x10, controller to PC, four u16 LE words. Meaning depends on the mode last selected on 0x40F, so it cannot be decoded per frame. Parameter extraction (2): [DIV, L_count, R_count, status 2|3]. PhasorSense (1): Word3 = phase 1/2/3, byte 4 = sensing mode, byte 5 = flag; phase 3 Words 0-2 = s16 x BaseVoltage/32768. Induction extraction (3): [count, ?, data_type, status 2|3].";
CM_ BO_ 1041 "Acquisition samples, base+0x11, controller to PC, four s16 LE words. Parameter extraction: R_count/2 frames of (current Sample0, voltage Sample1, current Sample2, voltage Sample3), scaled x/32768 x BaseCurrent / BaseVoltage, then L_count/2 frames with time = s16/DIV in Sample1/Sample3. PhasorSense: 500 frames, Word0 & 7 = hall state, Sample1..3 = phases A, B, C raw ADC. Induction extraction: two f32 LE per frame (bytes 0-3, 4-7); this signal layout does not decode those.";
CM_ BO_ 1042 "Transfer control, base+0x12, sent by both nodes. Four u16 LE words: Op, then three op-specific words. Read: REQUEST, INIT, PARAM_ACK, data on 0x414, BLOCK_ACK, (SIZE), CLOSE, CLOSE ack. Write: the same with the PC sending data, then a controller-initiated flash acknowledge on address 0x203. Op 0x4341 is not an op: it is the ACTMOT frame, ASCII 'ACTMOT' + motor index u16 LE, sent when the user selects a motor (effect on the controller unknown). Full description in ws22-config-transfer.dbc and wavesculptor22-config-protocol.md.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 Request_ResponderSends "1 the responder sends the data (read), 0 the initiator sends it (write).";
CM_ SG_ 1042 Init_Retries "Proposed retry limit. wsConfig 10; the controller 5 on the flash acknowledge.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 ParamAck_Retries "Agreed retry limit: the larger proposal.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 Request_Stream "1 stream (blob, ends with SIZE), 0 fixed size.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 ACTMOT_MotorIndex "Motor index selected in wsConfig (0-9).";
CM_ SG_ 1042 BlockAck_Toggle "Toggle bit of the block just accepted. A mismatching sender resends the block.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 Init_Timeout "Proposed timeout. wsConfig 1000 ms; the controller uses 250 ms on the flash acknowledge.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 ParamAck_Timeout "Agreed timeout: the larger proposal.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 Request_Size "Bytes to transfer. For stream transfers this is the window size, not the blob size.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 Init_BlockSize "Proposed block size. wsConfig uses 7 for fixed transfers and 140 for blobs.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 Close_Kind "0 close, 1 abort (retries exhausted), 2 close acknowledge.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 ParamAck_BlockSize "Agreed block size: the smaller proposal.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 BlockAck_Status "0 block received, 1 transfer complete.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 Request_Address "0x100-0x102 config blobs, 0x200-0x202 read-only info, 0x203 flash acknowledge (controller initiated), 0x400 reset.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 Size_Bytes "Stream end: the data sender announces a short last window; the receiver acknowledges with 0.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 ACTMOT_Tag "ASCII 'TMOT' (0x544F4D54 as u32 LE), the rest of the 'ACTMOT' tag.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 Op "Transfer opcode, multiplexor. 17217 (0x4341, bytes 'AC') marks an ACTMOT frame.";
CM_ BO_ 1044 "Transfer data, base+0x14, sent by both nodes. Byte 0: bit 7 toggle, bits 0-6 sequence in the block. Bytes 1-7 payload; frames per block = ceil(block/7), last frame zero padded. The payload meaning depends on the address in the preceding REQUEST. Blobs start with 'TRITIUM CONFIGURATION FILE'.";
CM_ SG_ 1044 Toggle "Starts at 0 and flips for each accepted block.";
CM_ SG_ 1044 Sequence "Frame index within the current block, from 0.";
CM_ BO_ 2015 "OBD-II functional broadcast. The utility sends 09 0B (identify) here for discovery. When the profile's ECU ID is 0x7F7 (AUTO), the reply to the profile commit arrives on 0x7D7+8 = 0x7DF, so a response-mode frame (mode >= 0x40) can also appear on this ID.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_ReadChecksum "u16 BE: mode + sum(4 PID bytes).";
CM_ SG_ 2015 FF_WriteAddress "Profile offset, u16 BE (profile is 3474 bytes).";
CM_ SG_ 2015 FF_ReadAddress "Profile offset of this 7C reply, u16 BE. Reply checksum = sum(4 PID bytes) + sum(data), mode excluded.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_ReadAddress "Profile offset, u16 BE.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_Detail "Commit failure code when ResponseCode = 0x40; the meanings are not in the utility.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 FF_Key "Upper 4 bytes of the 8-byte tier 2 key (BE); the lower 4 are in the next consecutive frame.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 FF_WriteLength "Chunk length (56, the last chunk shorter).";
CM_ SG_ 2015 FF_Seed "Upper 4 bytes of the 8-byte tier 2 seed (BE); the lower 4 are in the next consecutive frame.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_Key "Security key, u16 BE. Tier 1 key = seed XOR 0x1234. The tier 2 key (8 bytes) is multi-frame.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_WriteChecksum "u16 BE: mode + sub + sum(data bytes).";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_ReadLength "Bytes requested (56, the last chunk shorter).";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_Seed "Security seed, u16 BE. 0 = already unlocked.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_ResponseCode "72 accepted, 75 resend chunk, 77 bad checksum, 40 invalid (commit: SF_Detail = failure code), 21 busy, 33 access denied, 35 wrong key, 11 invalid mode, 22 (after 20 00) also counts as locked.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 FF_Pid16 "Live-data PID (mode 22/62). Value names from parameters.xml in BMSApp.jar.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 FF_SecurityLevel "5/6: tier 2 (password) seed/key; the 8-byte value follows. password = seed XOR key.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 FF_WriteSub "00 = 56-byte profile chunk: 3B 00 LL AAAA <LL bytes> <u16 checksum>.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 FF_Mode "Service mode of the multi-frame message.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_Pid8 "One-byte PID / sub-function of the mode. For 03/07/0A replies the DTC count.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_Pid16 "Live-data PID (mode 22/62) or mode 05/17 PID. Value names from parameters.xml in BMSApp.jar.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_InfoType "Mode 09 info type. 0B identify (also sent to 0x7DF), 04 firmware, 06 profile CRC, 0A serial, 0C loaded chips, 12 nickname, 13 hardware revision.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_LivePid8 "Mode 21/61 live-data PID. Value names from parameters.xml in BMSApp.jar.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_SecurityLevel "1/2 tier 1 seed/key, 5/6 tier 2 (password) seed/key.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_WriteSub "Write target. 03 commit (reply comes from the ECU ID in the NEW profile).";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_ReadSub "Always 00.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_RejectedMode "Mode this negative response / acknowledge refers to.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 SF_Mode "Service mode. Requests use the OBD-style modes; a positive response is mode + 0x40; 0x7F is a negative response or (for writes) an acknowledge.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 FF_Length "Total bytes of the multi-frame message after this byte (mode + PID + data).";
CM_ SG_ 2015 CF_Data "7 continuation bytes, big-endian so the hex reads in wire order.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 FC_BlockSize "The utility sends 30 07 00 ...; the sender then streams the rest with an 8 ms gap.";
CM_ SG_ 2015 PCI "Frame type. 1-7: single frame, value = 1 + PID length + data length. 0x10: first frame of a multi-frame message. 0x21-0x2F (wrapping to 0x20): consecutive frames, 7 data bytes each. 0x30: flow control, sent by the receiver on the opposite ID.";
CM_ BO_ 2019 "Requests to the BMS (profile ECU ID, default 0x7E3). OBD-II-like, not ISO-TP: single frame LL MM PID DATA (LL = 1 + PID len + data len, padded with 00); multi-frame 10 LL MM ..., then 21.. 2F (7 bytes each) after the BMS sends flow control 30 on 0x7EB. PID length depends on the mode (0: 03/04/07/0A, 2: 05/17/22, 3: 23, 4: 3C/A3, else 1). Configuration = the 3474-byte profile moved in 56-byte chunks: read with 3C, write with 3B 00 after 20 00, B2 03, tier 2 / tier 1 unlock (27), then commit 3B 03. Also carries the utility's live-data polling (22 F0xx, 21 xx, 01 01, B2 06 ...). The utility treats all IDs 0x700-0x7FF as diagnostic.";
CM_ SG_ 2019 SF_ReadChecksum "u16 BE: mode + sum(4 PID bytes).";
CM_ SG_ 2019 FF_WriteAddress "Profile offset, u16 BE (profile is 3474 bytes).";
