CM_ SG_ 2019 SF_ReadSub "Always 00.";
CM_ SG_ 2019 SF_RejectedMode "Mode this negative response / acknowledge refers to.";
CM_ SG_ 2019 SF_Mode "Service mode. Requests use the OBD-style modes; a positive response is mode + 0x40; 0x7F is a negative response or (for writes) an acknowledge.";
CM_ SG_ 2019 FF_Length "Total bytes of the multi-frame message after this byte (mode + PID + data).";
CM_ SG_ 2019 CF_Data "7 continuation bytes, big-endian so the hex reads in wire order.";
CM_ SG_ 2019 FC_BlockSize "The utility sends 30 07 00 ...; the sender then streams the rest with an 8 ms gap.";
CM_ SG_ 2019 PCI "Frame type. 1-7: single frame, value = 1 + PID length + data length. 0x10: first frame of a multi-frame message. 0x21-0x2F (wrapping to 0x20): consecutive frames, 7 data bytes each. 0x30: flow control, sent by the receiver on the opposite ID.";
CM_ BO_ 2021 "Third-party device configuration tunnelled by the OrionBMS 2 Utility (ScannerThirdPartySettingTxMode, fixed magic frames). Not analysed; raw bytes, big-endian so the hex reads in wire order. Not needed for BMS configuration.";
CM_ BO_ 2027 "Responses from the BMS (ECU ID + 8, default 0x7EB). Positive reply mode = request mode + 0x40; 7F xx yy = negative reply, or for writes the acknowledge (7F 3B 72 = chunk accepted). The utility sends flow control 30 07 00 .. on 0x7E3 after a first frame from here.";
